===Conjunction===
{{en-con}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a clause that is the object of a verb, especially a reporting verb or verb expressing belief, knowledge, perception, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|He told me '''that''' the book is a good read.}}
#: {{ux|en|I believe '''that''' it is true.''}}
#: {{ux|en|I can see '''that''' the ladder won't reach.''}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a clause that is the subject of a verb, especially the 'be' verb or a verb expressing judgement, opinion, etc.}}
## {{non-gloss definition|As delayed subject.}}
##: {{ux|en|It is almost certain '''that''' she will come.}}
##: {{ux|en|It amazes me '''that''' people still believe this nonsense.}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|_|literary}} {{non-gloss definition|As direct subject.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''That''' she will come is almost certain.}}
##: {{ux|en|'''That''' people still believe this nonsense amazes me.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a clause that complements an adjective or passive participle.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm sure '''that''' you are right.}}
#: {{ux|en|She is convinced '''that''' he is British.}}
## {{non-gloss definition|Expressing a reason or cause:}} [[because]], [[in that]].
##: {{ux|en|Be glad '''that''' you have enough to eat.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a subordinate clause modifying an adverb.}}
#: {{ux|en|Was John there? — Not '''that''' I saw.}}
#: {{ux|en|How often did she visit him? — Twice '''that''' I saw.}}
#* {{RQ:Trollope The Claverings|passage="{{...|Tell her from me," Lady Ongar had said, "that}} I will go anywhere '''that''' she may wish if she will go with me,"}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a clause that describes the information content of a preceding reporting noun.}}
#: {{ux|en|I heard a rumour '''that''' they got married.}}
#: {{ux|en|Reports '''that''' he left the country are circulating.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Introducing — especially, but not exclusively, with an antecedent like ''[[so]]'' or ''[[such]]'' — a subordinate clause expressing a result, consequence{{,}} or effect.}}
#: {{ux|en|The noise was so loud '''that''' she woke up.}}
#: {{ux|en|The problem was sufficiently important '''that''' it had to be addressed.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=w:Zoe Williams|title=I swore I wouldn't be an embarrassing mother. But the key to being a success in life is changing your mind, right?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140814182542/https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2008/may/23/familyandrelationships.women|date=23 May 2008
|passage=My dad apparently always said that no child of his would ever be harassed for its poor eating habits, and then I arrived, and I was so disgusting '''that''' he revised his opinion.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} {{non-gloss definition|Introducing a subordinate clause that expresses an aim, purpose{{,}} or goal ("final"), and usually contains the auxiliaries ''[[may]]'', ''[[might]]''{{,}} or ''[[should]]'':}} [[so]], [[so that]], [[in order that]].
